# polartouv

- Label: Polar to UV
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 4 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/polartouv.html
- Summary (EN): The Polar To UV node converts polar coordinates (distance and angle from an origin) into Cartesian coordinates, output as a uv layer or attribute. It recalculates each pixel's value in place and does not relocate pixels by itself.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Polar To UV convertit des coordonnées polaires en coordonnées UV cartésiennes, sans déplacer les pixels : il faut le chaîner avec UV Map et UV Sample.

- Inputs meaning: ["angle (optional): layer or attribute setting how far around the origin each point rotates", "length (optional): layer or attribute setting each point's distance from the origin"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Angle Units: Radians (unit circle), Degrees or Circles (0 to 1, where a full turn is 1)", "Angle: fallback angle when no angle input is wired", "Length: fallback distance from the origin when no length input is wired", "Output: uv, the Cartesian coordinates"]

- Caveats: ["Does not move pixels by itself. To relocate pixels, chain UV Map COP, then Polar to UV COP, then UV Sample COP."]

